    ('40063', 7, $$Wisdom was filled with alot of hunger ,how she was shouting at him but thoughts could not be able to heal the daughter.he then thought again what if i forgive her what will happen. Wisdom thought that forgiving could be the healer.$$),
    ('40063', 8, $$Wisdom forgave the Daughter and finally the daughter received the healing.the Rich Man was so happy that her daughter could be able resume her daily duties.$$),
    ('40074', 0, $$Once upon a time, in the small village of Machoka there lived an old man called Butere. Butere lived in a traditional house known as manyatta. He stayed always in this house because he was too old to walk.$$),
    ('40074', 1, $$Whenever Butere went in his bed to sleep during the night he could be disturbed by squeaks sound . This old man could not sleep comfortably in peace and never enjoyed his sleep.$$),
    ('40074', 2, $$One day ,Butere felt he could not tolerate anymore . "I must know where these sounds come from ",Butere said to himself in his old shaking voice.$$),
    ('40074', 3, $$Butere woke up that morning , supporting himself with his stick. He looked at his old blanket and noticed some holes. "ooh,this silly animal must be a rat! "The old Butere said angrily. I must teach this stupid animal a lesson today! ".$$),
    ('40074', 4, $$Butere proceeded to his store of his food and found that the rat had destroyed his cereals and maize. "Shame on you",the old Butere shouted angrily as if he was addressing anyone. That night Butere took a piece of ugali and poisoned it.$$),
    ('40074', 5, $$As usual Butere went to sleep. He heard the chirps sounds ,before even he could fall asleep. "it is the end of it today! "Butere whispered to himself. After a short while ,he heard a hissing sound. "it must be dying now! "the old man thought.$$),
    ('40074', 6, $$Butere slowly walked to where the trap was and found the rat dying helplessly "here you are",Butere shouted. He angrily bit the rat until it died. Since that day Butere was never disturbed again. He slept peacefully there after$$),
    ('40096', 0, $$Luntha loves bananas. Sadly, there are no bananas at the market. A big truck takes all the bananas to the city.$$),
    ('40096', 1, $$One day, Luntha asked his father, "Can't we grow our own bananas? " "That is a great idea! " Luntha's father replied. They quickly went to see a local farmer. They bought twenty suckers to start their own garden.$$),
    ('40096', 2, $$Luntha watered the banana plants every day. Three months later, the bananas developed broad leaves.$$),
    ('40096', 3, $$After nine months, the bananas started flowering. They produced big flower buds.$$),
    ('40096', 4, $$In the 10th month, the banana fingers grew bigger.$$),
    ('40096', 5, $$In the 12th month, the bananas were fully mature.$$),
    ('40096', 6, $$They harvested three plants. "We cannot eat all these bananas dad," said Luntha.$$),
    ('40096', 7, $$They refused to sell the bananas to the big truck. They took the extra bananas to the market. They made a lot of money at the market.$$),
    ('40170', 0, $$One day, Anansi the spider picked up some yams in his garden. They were very beautiful and very good yams, so he cooked them carefully on the fire. Then he sat down to eat them.$$),
    ('40170', 1, $$As Anansi was about to eat the first bite, he heard someone knock on the door. "Oh no ! " Anansi thought. "Who could it be? " But he opened the door. It was Turtle who looked very tired. "Anansi, please let me in. I've walked so far today and I'm so tired and hungry," Turtle said. So what could Anansi do except let him in?$$),
    ('40170', 2, $$Anansi was too selfish to share his beautiful and good yams with anyone. So he came up with a nasty plan. As Turtle sat down at the table and started reaching out to grab some yams, Anansi shouted at him, "Turtle, your hands are all dirty! You can't eat with your hands all dirty! Go wash them. " Turtle's hands were really dirty. So he crawled gently towards the river, washed his hands and then crawled back to the table.$$),
    ('40170', 3, $$But meanwhile, Anansi had started swallowing the yams. When Turtle returned, he saw that the yams were gone. Turtle looked at Anansi. "Thank you for inviting me to dinner. If you ever come near my house, come see me and let me make this dinner for you," he told her. And Turtle started crawling slowly towards his house.$$),
    ('40170', 4, $$After some time, Anansi began to think more and more about the free dinner promised by Turtle. So one day he went to Tortue. Anansi arrived at Turtle's house at dinner time as the sun was setting over the river. Turtle was lying on a rock in the sun, warming himself like turtles do. When Turtle saw Anansi, he said, "Hello, Anansi, did you come to eat with me? " And Anansi replied, "Yes, that would be very nice, thank you. " He was getting hungrier and hungrier.$$),
    ('40170', 5, $$So Turtle dived to the bottom of the river to set the table for dinner and get everything ready. Anansi waited on the rocks on the bank. Soon Turtle came swimming back and said, "Oh Anansi, it's ready now, come have dinner with me. " And Turtle dived again and started eating the green leaves prepared for dinner.$$),
    ('40170', 6, $$Anansi tried to dive to the bottom of the river, but it was a spider, not a turtle, and he couldn't dive that deep. He always came to the surface. He tried to jump into the river, he tried to dive, but nothing helped. He couldn't come down to eat that dinner.$$),
    ('40170', 7, $$Finally, Anansi had an idea. He put many stones in his coat pockets and was heavy enough to sink to the bottom of the river. How clever he was! He saw Turtle's table, full of juicy green leaves and lots of other delicious foods. Anansi's mouth was watering.$$),
    ('40170', 8, $$But just as Anansi grabbed some of that delicious food, Turtle stopped him. "Anansi, aren't you going to dinner with your coat on? We don't do that at home. " Anansi, without thinking, replied, "Oh, of course you're right, Turtle, what was I thinking? " He took off his coat.$$),
    ('40170', 9, $$But without the stones in his pockets to hold him down, Anansi immediately rose to the surface of the river and found himself out of the water. Anansi sadly put her head in the water and watched Turtle eat all the delicious food!$$),
    ('40191', 0, $$My name is Juma Shomari . I am nine years old. My father takes me to the bazaar every Saturday.$$),
    ('40191', 1, $$My father takes me to the bazaar every weekend. I like and enjoy shopping very much.$$),
    ('40191', 2, $$Shopping with my father is very fun. I am usually very happy. I meet many people here and learn many things$$),
    ('40191', 3, $$I love going on trips to the bazaar. Today I am shopping for my school uniforms.$$),
    ('40191', 4, $$I had so much fun shopping. I had a nice time today. See you all next time when we come back shopping again yaah!$$),
    ('40252', 0, $$It was a lovely day when two sisters Tasha and veronica were enjoying the view of nature . Tasha was the little sis and veronica was the elder one!$$),
    ('40252', 1, $$Whe they were sitting on the bench near the park. They wee now very astonished to see a thin band of rainbow stretching from the field to the the sky. It was a rainbow . All the kids were inspired by its colours$$),
    ('40252', 2, $$Tasha immediately suggested veronica to draw it for a long time memory. Veronica took her drawing book . And they drew the exact picture of a pretty rainbow!$$),
    ('40252', 3, $$Tasha grabbed the colour pencils and started adding some finishing touches. She drew colourful rainbows with people holding each other's hand$$),
    ('40252', 4, $$Now veronica drew a nice rainbow with people who were mesmerized with the colours. Tasha now drew two more characters and added finishing touches to the rainbow$$),
    ('40252', 5, $$They proved their creativity by drawing many forms of rainbow and they were appreciated dearly by their mother@And one day they said "I will next time draw the world"$$),
    ('40252', 6, $$Let's test you@How many colours does a rainbow have?@What was the elder sister's name?@Who drew a rainbow cloud?@Who were they appreciated by?$$),
    ('40252', 7, $$Read more books made by Dhivina$$),
    ('40311', 0, $$When Elephant ruled © Marvin Omondi 2022@ African storybook$$),
    ('40311', 1, $$Long long time ago when the lion was not the king of the jungle,in the savanna grasslands the mighty elephant ruled.$$),
    ('40311', 2, $$The elephant was given the position by tortoise the wise . Tortoise was a messenger of god and had power to elect a leader.$$),
    ('40311', 3, $$God of the animals had forbidden everyone from eating meat,all the animals ate grass. Every morning the leader of the animals was required to sing a song before every meal.$$),
    ('40311', 4, $$" All animals eat grass, no animal eat meat, cats and non cats" That was the song.@It happened that during the sunny period. Mr Buffalo,the step brother to the elephant had harvested honey.$$),
    ('40311', 5, $$Mr. Buffalo had made honey beer,when Elephant came over to his house,he drank alot of beer. In the morning,he was still drunk and he did not sing the song well.$$),
    ('40311', 6, $$"cats ..ea ..t..eat meat...animals eat grass.. elephant stammered. When the messenge reached god,god answered it by making all the cats to eat meat,the lion, leopard, cheetah and the panther.$$),
    ('40311', 7, $$The lion being the eldest in the cat family, became the leader. Until today the lion still roars as he rules the savanna grasslands.$$),
    ('40334', 0, $$This is Selsy. She likes talking about her style and how rich they are. She is popular because of her parents wealth. She is not as polite as other girls.$$),
    ('40334', 1, $$This is Kelsy,Selsy's twin sister. She is popular because of her polite altitude.$$),
    ('40334', 2, $$This is precious. She is poor but popular because of her beauty, everyone respects her because she respects herself.$$)
  ) AS v(source_id, page_index, text)
  JOIN books b
    ON b.source_platform = 'african_storybook' AND b.source_id = v.source_id
ON CONFLICT (book_id, page_index) DO NOTHING;

-- ───────── [적재검증] 트랜잭션 안 ─────────
-- (c) 적재 후 행 수 — 기대 382
SELECT count(*) AS rows_after FROM book_text bt
  JOIN books b ON b.id = bt.book_id
  WHERE b.source_platform='african_storybook' AND b.source_id IN ('37769', '37810', '37831', '37832', '37873', '37874', '37890', '37899', '38073', '38098', '38139', '38163', '38825', '38831', '38842', '38843', '38872', '38974', '38977', '39060', '39100', '39148', '39221', '39256', '39281', '39283', '39312', '39423', '39471', '39472', '39500', '39518', '39853', '39920', '39934', '39946', '39947', '40004', '40020', '40049', '40063', '40074', '40096', '40170', '40191', '40252', '40311', '40334');
-- (d) 조인 실패로 누락된 source_id — 기대 0행
SELECT v.source_id FROM (VALUES ('37769'), ('37810'), ('37831'), ('37832'), ('37873'), ('37874'), ('37890'), ('37899'), ('38073'), ('38098'), ('38139'), ('38163'), ('38825'), ('38831'), ('38842'), ('38843'), ('38872'), ('38974'), ('38977'), ('39060'), ('39100'), ('39148'), ('39221'), ('39256'), ('39281'), ('39283'), ('39312'), ('39423'), ('39471'), ('39472'), ('39500'), ('39518'), ('39853'), ('39920'), ('39934'), ('39946'), ('39947'), ('40004'), ('40020'), ('40049'), ('40063'), ('40074'), ('40096'), ('40170'), ('40191'), ('40252'), ('40311'), ('40334')) AS v(source_id)
  WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM books b
     WHERE b.source_platform='african_storybook' AND b.source_id=v.source_id);
-- (e) source 라벨 분포 — 기대 manifest_txt_v1 1종 / 382행
SELECT bt.source, count(*) FROM book_text bt JOIN books b ON b.id=bt.book_id
  WHERE b.source_platform='african_storybook' AND b.source_id IN ('37769', '37810', '37831', '37832', '37873', '37874', '37890', '37899', '38073', '38098', '38139', '38163', '38825', '38831', '38842', '38843', '38872', '38974', '38977', '39060', '39100', '39148', '39221', '39256', '39281', '39283', '39312', '39423', '39471', '39472', '39500', '39518', '39853', '39920', '39934', '39946', '39947', '40004', '40020', '40049', '40063', '40074', '40096', '40170', '40191', '40252', '40311', '40334')
  GROUP BY bt.source;
-- (f) page_index 축 검증 — 권마다 0부터 연속이어야 한다. 기대 0행(위반 없음)
SELECT b.source_id, min(bt.page_index) AS mn, max(bt.page_index) AS mx, count(*) AS n
  FROM book_text bt JOIN books b ON b.id=bt.book_id
  WHERE b.source_platform='african_storybook' AND b.source_id IN ('37769', '37810', '37831', '37832', '37873', '37874', '37890', '37899', '38073', '38098', '38139', '38163', '38825', '38831', '38842', '38843', '38872', '38974', '38977', '39060', '39100', '39148', '39221', '39256', '39281', '39283', '39312', '39423', '39471', '39472', '39500', '39518', '39853', '39920', '39934', '39946', '39947', '40004', '40020', '40049', '40063', '40074', '40096', '40170', '40191', '40252', '40311', '40334')
  GROUP BY b.source_id HAVING min(bt.page_index) <> 0 OR max(bt.page_index) <> count(*)-1;
-- (g) 빈 면 행 수 — 기대 0 (D7: 빈 면도 text='' 로 적재)
SELECT count(*) AS empty_rows FROM book_text bt JOIN books b ON b.id=bt.book_id
  WHERE b.source_platform='african_storybook' AND b.source_id IN ('37769', '37810', '37831', '37832', '37873', '37874', '37890', '37899', '38073', '38098', '38139', '38163', '38825', '38831', '38842', '38843', '38872', '38974', '38977', '39060', '39100', '39148', '39221', '39256', '39281', '39283', '39312', '39423', '39471', '39472', '39500', '39518', '39853', '39920', '39934', '39946', '39947', '40004', '40020', '40049', '40063', '40074', '40096', '40170', '40191', '40252', '40311', '40334') AND bt.text = '';

-- ───────── [종료] ─────────
-- (c)~(g)가 전부 기대값과 일치하면 아래 ROLLBACK; 을 COMMIT; 으로 바꿔 타이핑한다.
ROLLBACK;
